    "message": "Check new chunks for sensitive content from their bytes in Rust (stage B3)\n\nThe privacy check parsed and walked each new chunk in Python at every save. A kernel now\nreads the chunk's bytes and returns the distinct keys, and the distinct strings the\npatterns could match; the same Python functions decide on those. Every chunk not stored\nbefore is still checked, and without the extension the check is the same as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
