    },
    "message": "Hash Checkpoints as a tree over chunk hashes: Checkpoint v2 (stage B3)\n\nBoth hashes of a Checkpoint were the SHA-256 of the whole document, about 350 MB near\nday 7, computed at every save. In v2 a history list is hashed as its count and the\nSHA-256 of each 128 items, which are the archive's chunk keys, so a save hashes only new\nchunks; other values are leaves and objects on the path to a history hash their fields.\n\nv1 Checkpoints still load and verify under their own rule and can be replayed, resumed,\nforked and compared; what is saved after them is v2. The world, events and KPI hashes,\nwhich are computed from the documents, do not change. state_digest() follows the new\nrule, so previews still compare with a Checkpoint's state_hash.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
