    "message": "Check index rows from their bytes and send saved records to the indexer as bytes (stage B3)\n\nEach history index row was walked in Python for sensitive content; the kernel now reads\nits canonical JSON, and a row with something to check takes the old path. Saved EventLog\nrecords go to the indexing process as bytes, which it parses. A writer reads its Run's\nimmutable Scenario once, and an encoder remembers the sizes it computed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
