    },
    "message": "Write a computation's saves on their own thread (stage B3)\n\nA save spends most of its time waiting for fsync, which needs no GIL. The computation now\nhands each save to one thread and goes on: the same files, fsyncs and publication order,\neach save after the one before it. A failed save stops the computation at its next save\nor at its end, and the computation ends only once its saves are durable. fork and the\nother single saves stay synchronous.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
