    },
    "message": "Move only the disk writes of a save to its thread (stage B3)\n\nOn the thread, the Python work of a save shared the GIL with the ticks, and every stat\nof the usage measurement and every gzip call waited up to 5 ms to get it back: saves took\nabout a second and the computation waited for them. The checks, hashes and compression\nnow stay on the computation's thread; the thread only writes, syncs and publishes,\ncontinuing from the usage the save measured when it was prepared.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
